{
 "name": "cape_buffalo_bull",
 "description": "Old Cape buffalo bull ('dagga boy', Syncerus caffer caffer) standing, side view facing right, head a little low. Drawn fresh (not bison/water buffalo). Mid-charcoal #4a4440 hide, #34302d shading, #6a625c highlights, cracked dried-mud plates #9a8462 on flanks and legs, heavy ridged boss #2a2a2a, near horn droops down then hooks up (tip grey, about (182,-400)), ear hangs below the horn, dark wet muzzle, small flat stare, thin tail with tuft. Anchor bottom-centre, hooves on y=0, x -390..390, y -430..0. Back line smooth and flat from (-260,-330) to (+130,-340) for oxpeckers/cap; shoulder rise at x +170. Silhouette-safe (one outer shape).",
